WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.968 --> 00:00:02.234
-Today's Friday and that's

00:00:02.234 --> 00:00:03.834
usually when I catch up
on some personal stuff,

00:00:03.834 --> 00:00:06.000
you know, I check my inbox,
return some emails,

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:07.868
and, of course,
I send out thank-you notes.

00:00:07.868 --> 00:00:10.667
[ Cheering and applause ]
And I was just running
a bit behind today,

00:00:10.667 --> 00:00:11.834
so I thought,
if you guys wouldn't mind,

00:00:11.834 --> 00:00:12.968
I'd like to write out my weekly

00:00:12.968 --> 00:00:14.701
thank-you notes right now.
Is that cool?

00:00:14.701 --> 00:00:16.501
[ Cheering, whistling,
and applause ]

00:00:16.501 --> 00:00:19.067
James, can I get some thank-you
note writing music, please?

00:00:19.067 --> 00:00:21.334
-[ Playing tender tune ]
[ Laughter ]

00:00:21.334 --> 00:00:23.601
-That's my man.
-Christmas spirit came early.

00:00:23.601 --> 00:00:24.767
-Yeah, Christmas spirit,

00:00:24.767 --> 00:00:26.968
the Ghost of Christmas Present
right here.

00:00:26.968 --> 00:00:29.067
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah.

00:00:31.634 --> 00:00:32.968
♪♪

00:00:32.968 --> 00:00:34.467
Thank you, Taylor Swift,

00:00:34.467 --> 00:00:37.167
for giving us all more "Red."

00:00:37.167 --> 00:00:39.167
And thank you, People magazine,
for giving us all

00:00:39.167 --> 00:00:40.300
more Rudd.

00:00:40.300 --> 00:00:42.000
[ Cheering and applause ]
-Oh, yeah!

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:43.133
-That's my dude!

00:00:45.367 --> 00:00:48.501
-Come on.

00:00:48.501 --> 00:00:50.033
♪♪
[ Laughter ]

00:00:50.033 --> 00:00:52.734
-Thank you,
"Red (Taylor's Version),"

00:00:52.734 --> 00:00:54.601
[ Cheering and applause ]
for being the music
world's version

00:00:54.601 --> 00:00:56.467
of labeling your food
in the office fridge.

00:00:56.467 --> 00:00:58.968
[ Cheering and applause ]
It's like, "That's mine."

00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:02.801
"That's its says,
'Todd's rice pudding.'"

00:01:02.801 --> 00:01:04.734
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:04.734 --> 00:01:07.033
"Ugh!"
-"Agh!

00:01:07.033 --> 00:01:09.400
You don't even
understand my life."

00:01:09.400 --> 00:01:11.167
[ Laughter ]
-"I sit at home,

00:01:11.167 --> 00:01:13.100
make rice pudding,
I bring it in

00:01:13.100 --> 00:01:14.634
and you animals eat it!"

00:01:14.634 --> 00:01:16.701
[ Laughter ]

00:01:16.701 --> 00:01:18.000
♪♪
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:20.234
-Thank you, "Dexter: New Blood,"

00:01:20.234 --> 00:01:22.300
for premiering
on Showtime this week.

00:01:22.300 --> 00:01:23.701
Or, as "Squid Game" put it,

00:01:23.701 --> 00:01:25.634
"Oh, you murder
one person each episode?

00:01:25.634 --> 00:01:26.701
That's cu-u-u-te."

00:01:26.701 --> 00:01:29.667
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:31.334 --> 00:01:32.567
♪♪

00:01:32.567 --> 00:01:34.567
Thank you, Thanksgiving,

00:01:34.567 --> 00:01:35.968
for being the one day
in November

00:01:35.968 --> 00:01:38.067
we don't spend preparing
for Christmas.

00:01:38.067 --> 00:01:40.400
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:01:40.400 --> 00:01:42.367
I can't wait for Christmas.

00:01:42.367 --> 00:01:44.200
-I don't care what anybody says.
I like Christmas.

00:01:44.200 --> 00:01:46.968
[ Laughter ]

00:01:46.968 --> 00:01:48.868
-Okay.

00:01:48.868 --> 00:01:49.968
♪♪

00:01:49.968 --> 00:01:52.167
Thank you, crossword puzzles,

00:01:52.167 --> 00:01:53.400
for being
the most frustrating way

00:01:53.400 --> 00:01:55.267
to remind myself
that I'm an idiot.

00:01:55.267 --> 00:01:56.701
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:56.701 --> 00:01:57.868
I don't know any
of these things.

00:02:00.801 --> 00:02:02.801
"Blank Fallon,
host of 'The Tonight Show.'"

00:02:02.801 --> 00:02:04.033
-"I have no idea."

00:02:04.033 --> 00:02:05.634
[ Laughter ]

00:02:05.634 --> 00:02:06.834
-It's you, you dummy!

00:02:06.834 --> 00:02:08.300
[ Laughter ]
-Oh, ma'am!

00:02:08.300 --> 00:02:09.968
[ Laughter ]

00:02:09.968 --> 00:02:11.634
It's your name, dummy!

00:02:11.634 --> 00:02:14.200
[ Laughter ]

00:02:14.200 --> 00:02:17.501
My mom and dad, when we
first got "The Tonight Show,"

00:02:17.501 --> 00:02:18.834
they watched
some local news show

00:02:18.834 --> 00:02:21.734
and they had a trivia
question thing about me

00:02:21.734 --> 00:02:23.200
and they were answering the TV.

00:02:23.200 --> 00:02:24.367
-Oh.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:24.367 --> 00:02:25.801
-It's like "His first --"
and they're like,

00:02:25.801 --> 00:02:26.968
"Saugerties High School!"

00:02:26.968 --> 00:02:28.234
[ Laughter ]
It's like,

00:02:28.234 --> 00:02:29.534
"This isn't for you, this game."

00:02:29.534 --> 00:02:30.634
[ Aww and laughter ]

00:02:30.634 --> 00:02:33.968
But, yeah.
-Yeah.

00:02:33.968 --> 00:02:36.434
[ Laughter ]

00:02:36.434 --> 00:02:39.000
-Anyway.

00:02:39.000 --> 00:02:40.367
Never mind.
-Yeah.

00:02:40.367 --> 00:02:41.501
Well, no, wait, what?

00:02:41.501 --> 00:02:43.567
-Agh! [ Laughs ]
-No.

00:02:43.567 --> 00:02:45.100
No, what is it? What is it?
-I'm good.

00:02:45.100 --> 00:02:46.200
It's just --

00:02:46.200 --> 00:02:47.667
Moving on. Never mind.
-You seem upset.

00:02:47.667 --> 00:02:49.367
-No, I'm fine.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:49.367 --> 00:02:51.000
-Oh, come on.
Don't be that way.

00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:52.367
What is it?
-No, no, have a good time.

00:02:52.367 --> 00:02:54.234
The party's fun, man.
Thanks for having me.

00:02:54.234 --> 00:02:55.801
I'm going to take you with me.
We're having a party.

00:02:55.801 --> 00:02:57.734
No, no, no. You can stay.
What's the matter?

00:02:57.734 --> 00:02:59.400
-Well, I just haven't
talked to my dad.

00:02:59.400 --> 00:03:00.567
-What about?

00:03:00.567 --> 00:03:01.667
-Fifteen years.

00:03:01.667 --> 00:03:03.267
[ Suspenseful-melancholy
tune plays ]

00:03:03.267 --> 00:03:05.334
It all happened
because it was Christmas Eve.

00:03:05.334 --> 00:03:07.934
-Yeah?
[ Laughter ]

00:03:07.934 --> 00:03:10.667
-Oh, no.
What happened?

00:03:10.667 --> 00:03:12.300
-I didn't tell you?
-No.

00:03:12.300 --> 00:03:14.200
-This is insane.

00:03:14.200 --> 00:03:16.100
My grandma...
-Right.

00:03:16.100 --> 00:03:17.868
I know.
I love your grandma.

00:03:17.868 --> 00:03:19.434
I just saw her --
-Boy, my dad loved

00:03:19.434 --> 00:03:20.801
his own mother, sure.
-Yeah.

00:03:20.801 --> 00:03:22.434
[ Laughter ]

00:03:22.434 --> 00:03:23.934
-We we're drinking, you know.
-Sure.

00:03:23.934 --> 00:03:25.367
Christmas --
-Christmas Eve, sure.

00:03:25.367 --> 00:03:27.901
She had -- She had this wig on
and everything,

00:03:27.901 --> 00:03:29.267
that matched the candles.

00:03:29.267 --> 00:03:32.033
It was blue and silver.
It was funny.

00:03:32.033 --> 00:03:33.934
We were just having fun
and I guess she forgot

00:03:33.934 --> 00:03:35.934
to take her pills or something.
-Right.

00:03:35.934 --> 00:03:38.734
♪♪

00:03:38.734 --> 00:03:40.033
Can we turn the cameras off?

00:03:40.033 --> 00:03:41.601
[ Jingling bells join music ]
[ Laughter ]

00:03:41.601 --> 00:03:42.634
She, uh...

00:03:42.634 --> 00:03:45.968
[ Laughter ]
♪♪

00:03:45.968 --> 00:03:47.901
...staggers out of the house.
-Right.

00:03:47.901 --> 00:03:49.434
Drunk as a skunk, which is fine.
-Crazy-drunk,

00:03:49.434 --> 00:03:52.367
embarrassingly drunk, yeah.
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:03:52.367 --> 00:03:54.901
Uh,

00:03:54.901 --> 00:03:56.200
we didn't hear from her
the next day.

00:03:56.200 --> 00:03:57.567
[ Laughter ]

00:03:57.567 --> 00:03:59.501
She disappeared?
What --

00:03:59.501 --> 00:04:00.567
-I found her.

00:04:00.567 --> 00:04:01.767
-Where?

00:04:01.767 --> 00:04:03.100
-Right in front of the house.

00:04:03.100 --> 00:04:04.200
[ Laughter ]

00:04:04.200 --> 00:04:06.000
Grandma had been run over
by a reindeer.

00:04:06.000 --> 00:04:07.234
[ Laughter and applause ]
-Oh, my God.

00:04:07.234 --> 00:04:09.133
♪♪

00:04:09.133 --> 00:04:10.467
Where?

00:04:10.467 --> 00:04:12.734
-Walking home, from our house.

00:04:12.734 --> 00:04:13.934
-On Christmas Eve?

00:04:13.934 --> 00:04:15.934
[ Laughter ]
-There were hoof--

00:04:15.934 --> 00:04:18.300
Her bare back was exposed.
-Right.

00:04:18.300 --> 00:04:20.300
[ Laughter ]
♪♪

00:04:20.300 --> 00:04:22.567
Somehow, her dress
had been ripped off.

00:04:22.567 --> 00:04:23.667
[ Laughter ]
-Oh, my God!

00:04:23.667 --> 00:04:24.868
-There were hoove marks --

00:04:24.868 --> 00:04:26.434
-Hoove marks on her back?
-Hoove marks on her back.

00:04:26.434 --> 00:04:28.834
-Oh, my God!
What kind of animals did this?

00:04:28.834 --> 00:04:30.400
Reindeer, apparently.
-Yeah.

00:04:30.400 --> 00:04:33.167
[ Laughter ]
♪♪

00:04:33.167 --> 00:04:34.534
-You can say

00:04:34.534 --> 00:04:36.567
you don't believe in Santa.
-Right, but your grandpa,

00:04:36.567 --> 00:04:37.834
I know he's a man of faith.

00:04:37.834 --> 00:04:39.534
[ Laughter ]
♪♪

00:04:39.534 --> 00:04:41.300
-Man of faith, yeah.

00:04:41.300 --> 00:04:42.868
We still believe in Santa, yeah.

00:04:42.868 --> 00:04:44.300
[ Laughter ]
Anyway. [ Clears throat ]

00:04:44.300 --> 00:04:45.367
Can't believe I didn't
tell you that.

00:04:45.367 --> 00:04:49.400
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:04:49.400 --> 00:04:50.601
-Aww.

00:04:50.601 --> 00:04:52.267
[ Laughter ]

00:04:52.267 --> 00:04:53.400
-[ Playing tender tune ]

00:04:53.400 --> 00:04:55.501
-Thank you, cider doughnuts,

00:04:55.501 --> 00:04:57.467
for being regular doughnuts
that are like,

00:04:57.467 --> 00:04:59.200
"Um, we're not like
other doughnuts."

00:04:59.200 --> 00:05:02.367
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:04.634 --> 00:05:05.767
♪♪
[ Laughter ]

00:05:05.767 --> 00:05:07.400
Thank you, goatees,

00:05:07.400 --> 00:05:09.501
for being the sweater vest
of beards.

00:05:09.501 --> 00:05:11.467
There you have it, everybody.
Those are my "Thank You Notes."

